2a:["$","p","p-9",{"children":"Suppose the available dataset contains 20,000 tickets from January through June. A defensible first experiment might train on January–April, choose settings on May, and test once on June. If a large incident generated hundreds of nearly identical tickets across those months, group the incident so related examples cannot appear on both sides of a split. Report the size and class distribution of every set; a tiny access-support class may need separate error analysis."}]
2b:["$","h2","h2-5",{"id":"try-it","children":"Try it"}]
2c:["$","p","p-10",{"children":["Take ten representative records and mark every candidate feature as ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"available at prediction"}],", ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"created later"}],", or ",["$","strong","strong-2",{"children":"uncertain"}],". Draft a label policy. Choose a split strategy and write one sentence explaining the future situation it tests. List two ways the measured score could still overstate production quality."]}]
2d:["$","h2","h2-6",{"id":"check-your-understanding","children":"Check your understanding"}]
2e:["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Why is “the team that resolved the ticket” dangerous as an input feature?"}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"When is a time-based or grouped split preferable to a random row split?"}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"What happens if you compare model versions on the test set every day?"}],"\n"]}]
2f:["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Answer guide:"}]," the feature may only exist after the prediction; grouped or time splits test unseen entities or future changes; repeated test use leaks selection into the final estimate."]}]
